Ghostscript (AGPL)
================================================================================
Project: https://www.ghostscript.com/
License: see GHOSTSCRIPT-LICENSE.txt (GNU Affero General Public License v3)

Pinned Windows build (see scripts/fetch-sidecars.ps1):
  Ghostscript 10.05.1 (tag gs10051), Windows x64
  Binary we unpack: gs10051w64.exe from Artifex downloads
  Upstream release: https://github.com/ArtifexSoftware/ghostpdl-downloads/releases/tag/gs10051

Redistribution (summary — AGPL v3 controls):
  - Windows installs of Converte Fácil may include Ghostscript binaries under
    the app resources (`sidecars/ghostscript/`).
  - Ghostscript remains AGPL-licensed software. Recipients of the installer are
    entitled to the corresponding source for that Ghostscript version.
  - Corresponding source for the pinned release is offered by Artifex at the
    release page above (GhostPDL / Ghostscript source archives for 10.05.1).
    If that page moves, use the version pin in scripts/fetch-sidecars.ps1 to
    locate the matching Artifex source tarball.
  - Converte Fácil does not modify Ghostscript; it runs `gswin64c` as a separate
    process (via ImageMagick PDF delegates). The Converte Fácil application
    source is not part of the Ghostscript program.

If you redistribute Converte Fácil builds that include Ghostscript, you must
also respect AGPL obligations for that component (including offering
corresponding source for the Ghostscript version you ship).

================================================================================
LibreOffice (downloaded during setup; not embedded in the NSIS payload)
================================================================================
Documents mode needs LibreOffice (`soffice`). The Converte Fácil NSIS package does
not embed the ~350 MB LibreOffice MSI. After installing app files, the setup may
download a pinned MSI from Document Foundation and silent-install it
(see scripts/install-libreoffice-setup.ps1 and src-tauri/windows/hooks.nsh).

Pinned Windows MSI (bump carefully; keep SHA256 in sync with winget):
  LibreOffice 26.2.4 Win x86-64
  https://download.documentfoundation.org/libreoffice/stable/26.2.4/win/x86_64/LibreOffice_26.2.4_Win_x86-64.msi
  SHA256: 202f26cda071c5aa4996a5a28412fddceb3891dceb0366982c62650456c0730f

In-app fallback: winget (`TheDocumentFoundation.LibreOffice`) or the official
download page. Strategy: docs/adr/0002-libreoffice-strategy.md
LibreOffice license overview: https://www.libreoffice.org/licenses/

